From: netrunner <299844489+plotarmordev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:09:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drama: int3 routed experts (3.5 bits) in the CUDA NVFP4
 expert kernel, and their GPTQ packer

A layer whose gate codes are [n, 3k/8] bytes is int3: each 16-input block is
three little-endian u16 planes (sign, hi, lo) for the E2M1 magnitudes 0, 2, 4
and 6, under NVFP4's E4M3 block-16 scales and FP32 global. The loader packs
them into 112-word blocks (three code planes, the unchanged 16 scale words);
tf_int3_gate_up_f32 and tf_int3_down_f32 rebuild each lane's E2M1 nibbles
from the planes and run NVFP4's decode body, whose 4-bit instantiations are
unchanged. Prompt rows refuse int3 (OptionNotBuilt) as they refuse Drama's
NVFP4 SwiGLU.

drama_nvfp4_gptq.py --mode int3 --provenance nvfp4-provenance.json quantizes
the FP8 originals with each layer's published GPTQ kappa, damping and routed
counts, refusing rows whose counts differ, and records the provenance sha256.
